    "q-14739": {
      "dom_id": "step-q14739",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int (3{x}^{2}+2){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3{x}^{2}+2\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+2){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+2)(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+2){e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{6}{3}\\int x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+2){e}^{3x}}{3}-2\\int x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}(3x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+2){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+2){e}^{3x}}{3}-2(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}(3x-1)+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+2){e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{9}(3x-1)-2D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}(3(3{x}^{2}+2)-2(3x-1))-2D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}(9{x}^{2}-6x+8)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2D.$",
